<title>USA: Alliant Techsystems wins rocket motor order.</title>
<headline>Alliant Techsystems wins rocket motor order.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliant Techsystems Inc said Thursday it will participate in a contract from the U.S. Defense Deparment to produce parts for a new type of air-to-air missile that could eventually be worth up to $100 million.</p>
<p>Alliant said its Tactical Business Unit will make the solid propulsion rocket motor and thrust vector control system for the AIM-9X short-range missile. Alliant said the initial contract, worth $50 million, is part of a larger pact between the Pentagon and Hughes Electronics Corp.</p>
<p>Alliant is an aerospace and defense company.</p>
<p>Its shares were down 1/8 Thursday afternoon at 52-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
